+
+### 30. Final apply-pack release rules distilled from the July 2026 pass
+`DISTILLED` · `ALL`
+
+These rules are the standing release contract for every active apply pack. They were
+distilled from 81 correction signals across 55 apply-pack sessions and repeated visual
+and QA checks.
+
+**Research is the foundation.** Every CV, cover letter, and form-fields file must be
+directly informed by the job description, hiring-manager or role-level intel, company
+context, and the strongest documented proof in the prior CV. Do not draft from a generic
+career narrative when role-specific evidence exists.
+
+**Protect ATS while polishing.** Preserve searchable role language, measurable outcomes,
+clear section labels, normal Markdown structure, and extractable PDF text. Typography
+changes belong in the shared print stylesheet; never solve visual density by deleting
+evidence, shrinking body copy, or weakening the writing-craft pass.
+
+**Projects are proof surfaces.** Use no more than the strongest role-resonant projects,
+and hyperlink the project or claim itself to the matching artifact, video, timeline entry,
+or story on thestorytellermitch.com. Never print a raw URL beside the linked phrase.
+
+**Writing samples rotate by role.** Keep the VP voice essay for executive-communications
+and AI-voice roles. Prefer the AJ+ measles script for communications and editorial roles,
+and the Google Day-One orientation script for internal and corporate communications roles.
+Do not let three interchangeable Substack links crowd out a stronger script or artifact.
+
+**Use exact, defensible experience language.** Distinguish newsroom people management
+from the last eight years of IC and program leadership. Describe the xGE audience as the
+company-wide community of 1,000+ Principal, Distinguished, and Fellow Sr. Tech ICs. Use
+tracked or designed impact metrics with the status labeled. Do not invent adoption,
+ranking-team, Tableau, fintech, aerospace, or formal people-management claims.
+
+**Use the approved terminology.** Write `Sr. Tech IC` or `Sr. Tech ICs` when referring to
+the senior technical audience. Write `executive communications`, `senior engineering`,
+and `senior IC` without incorrect hyphenation, except where a true grammatical compound
+requires it. Keep the candidate contact line exactly `Open to relocation`.
+
+**Apply-pack typography is shared and testable.** The descriptor under the name must be
+visibly larger than body text. Employer/date lines, experience summary lines, and the
+Earlier Career newsroom summary must match the body bullet size. Experience summaries are
+italic muted charcoal. Summary paragraphs receive a clean uninterrupted line break.
+Hide web-only controls such as the SOUND toggle from PDFs. After any source edit, render
+again, verify Markdown timestamps precede PDFs, spot-check visuals, and run the zero-failure
+PDF QA gate.
+
+**Evidence:** “research is robust and bulletproof”; “the project links do not look good”; “I
+won't lie or stretch that”; “the line under my earlier newsroom experience should be the
+same size as the summary line underneath the google experiences”; “give me a clean
+uninterrupted line break between each paragraph.”
